  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1... \nWe will see an increase in moisture Sunday especially with mid \nand high clouds from a Nor'easter. Areas closest to the \nAppalachian ridge- line could see a chance for light rain. \nEastern Ohio will remain far enough west to remain mostly sunny \nsky. With the increased cloud cover, daytimes highs drop back \ninto the upper 60s on Sunday.\n\nPrecipitation is possible on Wednesday into Thursday when the \nridge breaks down allowing a shortwave trough passage. As of \nnow, the probability of measured precipitation remains between \n30%-40% based on the weak forcing with this feature and a \nrelatively dry atmosphere. Probability of 24 hour QPF >=0.10\" \nreside between 20%-30%.",
